# Read-only, enforced twice: the playbook asks, the platform enforces.
# Render: see diagrams/README.md.

vars: { d2-config: { pad: 24 } }

direction: right

ask: A request that\nwould write data {
  class: source
  shape: person
}

playbook: Layer 1: the playbook\nUC skill rule: "Read only.\nNever run INSERT, … DROP, or ALTER." {
  class: store
}

policy: Layer 2: the CEL guardrail\nOmnigent, before the tool runs:\none SELECT · WITH · SHOW · DESCRIBE · EXPLAIN,\nno write keyword, a string query {
  class: govern
}

sql: Databricks SQL MCP\nthen the SQL warehouse {
  class: serve
  icon: ${ICONS}/databricks/sql_warehouse.svg
  icon.near: bottom-center
  label.near: top-center
}

refused: The agent refuses\n"CREATE TABLE …" {
  class: source
  style.stroke-dash: 4
}

denied: Denied by policy\n"SET …", "EXPLAIN WITH … INSERT" {
  class: source
  style.stroke-dash: 4
}

ask -> playbook
playbook -> policy: a tool call it chose to make
policy -> sql: allowed { class: accent }
playbook -> refused: stops here
policy -> denied: never reaches the warehouse
